Agricultural approaches and practices that contribute to climate change mitigation
There are many different approaches and practices for sustainable crop production that can contribute to climate 
change mitigation. As with climate change adaptation, these approaches and practices can provide options for location-specific contexts and should be adapted with local farmers/farming communities. 
Examples include:
•	conservation agriculture;
•	soil compaction management;
•	improved farming systems with several crop rotations; 
•	crop diversification;
•	promotion of legumes in crop rotations;
•	growing cover crops;
•	mulch cropping;
•	restoration of cultivated peaty soils and degraded lands;
•	soil management practices that reduce fertilizer use (e.g. urea deep placement);
•	integrated nutrient management;
