Good practices to manage and reduce bycatch and discards
Bycatch can be managed and discards can be reduced through, among others: •	input and control measures;
•	special and/or temporal measures;
•	design improvements and use of fishing gear and bycatch reduction devices (e.g. mesh and hook size, turtle excluder devices);
•	use of operational techniques that reduce bycatch (i.e. backdown manoeuvre during purse-seining); 
•	use of techniques that increase the survival rate of the released catches; and
•	use of vessel and fishing gear position monitoring and habitat mapping systems 
(FAO, 2011c). 
